{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/49791.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS WMID-3FE965: Staffordshire Moorlands Patera composite image"]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["oggetto"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (oggetto)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["100-199 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Staffordshire (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["A 'patera' or handled pan, known as 'The Staffordshire Pan', cast in copper alloy with elaborate enamelled decoration and a Latin inscription below the rim. The body of the vessel is convex and c.2mm thick, and the slightly out-turned rim has a rounded edge, with an external diameter of 89.5mm. There is a diagonal foot-ring with a diameter of 54mm and an internal ledge cast at c.1mm from the base edge, onto which the missing base would have been soldered. Traces of the solder survive on this ledge. The handle is now missing, but judging from other finds it is likely to have been flat and bow-tie shaped and also inlaid with coloured enamel. There are the remains of the solder used to affix…"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["WMID-3FE965"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["49791"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: Stuart Laidlaw, Sally Worrell, 2003-09-29 15:25:39, CC BY-SA 2.0 ; Stuart Laidlaw, Nick Herepath, 2003-09-29 15:25:39, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/49791","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS WMID-3FE965: Staf